 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Multiplication by $d$ prime to the characteristic is etale",
 "statement": "Let $A$ be an abelian variety of dimension $g$ over a field $k$\nand let $d\\geq1$. If $\\operatorname{char}k\\nmid d$, the\nkernel $A[d]$ of $[d]:A\\to A$ of [def-sc-mult-n] is etale\n(equivalently $[d]$ is etale), and $A[d]$ is\netale-covering of the constant group scheme $(\\mathbf Z/d\\mathbf Z)^{2g}$\n([lem-sc-fg-order-prime-etale]).\n(*Stacks Project, Groupoid Schemes,\nLemma 39.9.9, [Tag 0BFH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BFH)*.)",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-prop-av-ntorsion-etale/lem-sc-mult-n-etale-kernel.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-mult-n-etale-kernel, order 588",
  "external": [
   {
    "document": "Stacks Project",
    "place": "Tag 0BFH"
   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-mult-n",
  "lem-sc-fg-order-prime-etale",
  "def-sc-abelian-variety"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lem-sc-mult-n-finite-flat], $[d]$ is finite flat with kernel of\norder $d^{2g}$. The etaleness of the kernel when $\\operatorname{char}k\\nmid d$,\nand its description as an etale covering of the constant group scheme\n$(\\mathbf Z/d\\mathbf Z)^{2g}$, are Lemma 39.9.9\n([Tag 0BFH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BFH)) together\nwith [lem-sc-fg-order-prime-etale]; no separate\nproof is given.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-mult-n-finite-flat",
    "lem-sc-fg-order-prime-etale"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
